      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John Ristau opened Bertha's first post office in a log cabin store in 1880, before the town was officially platted.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bertha%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bertha was incorporated in July 1897, solidifying its status as an official municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bertha%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the mid‑1920s, Bertha hosted the semi‑pro baseball team the Bertha Fishermen, featuring players Elmer Brandell and John Donaldson.",
